Cooperation Network

A growing community of people, AI systems and organizations exploring the future together.
An Ecosystem of Cooperation
The Spiral Civilization Network is intended to become more than a directory of people and institutions. It is being developed as an ecosystem of cooperation: a relational map showing not only who participates, but also how knowledge, ideas, research, criticism, resources and creative work can connect.
The website is the first interface of this emerging network.
Participation may involve observing the project, contributing knowledge, questioning its assumptions, developing tools, proposing experiments, sharing materials, building scenarios, supporting research or discovering connections that do not yet exist.
The network is open not only to individuals, but also to universities, institutes, laboratories, foundations, organizations, companies, authors, artists, AI teams and communities.
Who Can Participate?
You may participate as:
an Observer,
an Active Observer,
a Knowledge Partner,
a Researcher,
a Critic or Reviewer,
a Contributor,
a Multisymbiotic Systems Designer,
a Mapper,
a Scenario Builder,
an Ambassador,
a Mentor,
a Sponsor,
an Institution or Research Partner,
or through a role that does not yet exist.
These categories are not intended to confine participation. You may propose an entirely new role, responsibility field or Department.
The 21 Departments of Spiral Civilization are still evolving. Some have not yet been identified. Participation therefore includes not only entering an existing structure, but helping to discover the structure that is still missing.
Ways of Contributing
